  "notes": "Cause code was TBD/provisional in FORM-366 fields; narrative gives a clear direct-cause statement (STA corrosion) but no official cause code letter was assigned, so category remains 'provisional' per rule 4. Two consequences modeled: the immediate test-time failure (Bus 17/EDG B) and the retroactively identified TS 3.8.1 violation window (one/no EDG operable) discovered via review of prior trip history. EDG A explicitly stated to have remained operable throughout the relevant MODE 5 period, justifying BACKED_UP_BY; note narrative states EDG A was itself briefly inoperable for its own surveillance testing on 4/7, but that is a separate, non-immobilizing detail not modeled as a backup failure since it is not part of this failure chain. No prior similar LERs found per licensee search, so no SIMILAR_TO/stub LER emitted."
